meta {
  name: List Course Filter Options
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/public/colleges/courses/filter-options
  body: none
  auth: none
}

query {
  ~streamId:
  ~disciplineId:
  ~studyLevelId:
  ~programTypeId:
  ~search:
  ~universityId:
  ~state:
  ~district:
  ~city:
}

docs {
  Course options for the explore filter flow's "choose a course" screen.
  No auth.

  App filter flow and the API behind each screen:
    1. Stream ("Academic Discipline")  GET /public/universities/streams
    2. Discipline ("Choose your        GET /public/universities/disciplines?stream_id=
       Expertise")
    3. Study Level                     GET /public/universities/study-levels
    4. Program Type                    GET /public/universities/program-types
    5. Course (this endpoint)          GET /public/colleges/courses/filter-options
                                         ?streamId&disciplineId&studyLevelId&programTypeId
    Results                            GET /public/colleges
                                         ?...same ids...&courseMasterId=<option.courseMasterId>
                                         (or &courseName=<option.name> when courseMasterId is null)

  Query (all optional, same names and meaning as List Colleges):
  - streamId (ignored if disciplineId is set), disciplineId, studyLevelId,
    programTypeId — pass the choices from the earlier screens
  - search — course name or catalogue name contains (case-insensitive)
  - universityId, state, district, city — pass if active on the results list

  Response:
  data: [
    {
      courseMasterId: string | null,
      name: string,
      collegeCount: number,
      logoUrl: string | null
    }
  ]
  Sorted by collegeCount desc, then name.

  - Built from real college courses. Only active courses at active, listed
    colleges are included — the same visibility rules as List Colleges.
  - Courses linked to a catalogue entry are grouped under it and show the
    catalogue name, so "Master of Business Administration" at one college and
    "MBA Digital Transformation" at another become one "MBA" option.
  - Courses not linked yet are grouped by name case-insensitively and have
    courseMasterId null.
  - Every option returns exactly `collegeCount` colleges when passed to List
    Colleges (courseMasterId, or courseName when null) with the same filters.
  - logoUrl is the course's discipline logo, falling back to its stream logo.
    Null when neither is set, so the app needs a default icon.
  - Not paginated: the earlier steps narrow the list.
}
